text:
marta: Pushed a lightweight Figma pass for the 'nocturne' console theme — link: https://www.figma.com/file/zzz/nocturne-theme

marta: Notes: base #07090C, panel #0B0F12, code-surface #0C1014. Main worries: tiny heatmap tiles bleeding on high-saturation reds and keyboard-focus visibility on inline chart controls.

elliot: Really clean. Two quick items: 1) chart gridlines are too faint at 0.10 alpha; fails small text AA. 2) tooltip hover only on donut segments — needs keyboard affordance.

raj: On heatmap colors, avoid pure reds at endpoints. Suggest endpoints: low #22323A, mid #3F6E7C, high #E96A57. Also add a noncolor texture for bottom buckets (thin diagonal hatch).

marta: Agreed. I'll add a hatch option in Figma: 1px lines, 40% opacity, 45deg spacing. Will also include an explicit numeric label on hover for print.

elliot: For code tokens at 12px, tone down yellow strings. Try #D9A35A for strings and #73C9FF for keywords. Make keywords 600 weight in code to help separation.

sam: Ran axe on the prototype: flagged sparklines (1px) and hover-only tooltips. Also found legend items without focus outline when tabbing.

raj: Fixes: increase sparkline stroke to 1.5px, stroke-linecap round, opacity 0.95. Add tabindex=0 to interactive SVG elements and mirror :focus to :hover styles with 3px ring (color #88E6FF at 0.9).

marta: Dropping CSS tokens to sync with tokens repo — will push branch after we agree.

marta: ```css
:root {
  --nocturne-bg: #07090C;
  --nocturne-surface: #0B0F12;
  --code-surface: #0C1014;
  --text-primary: #E7F3F6;
  --code-string: #D9A35A;
  --code-keyword: #73C9FF;
  --link: #6ED7DB;
  --heat-low: #22323A;
  --heat-mid: #3F6E7C;
  --heat-high: #E96A57;
}
```

elliot: Also small UX nit — use #F6FBFD for tooltip copy (not pure white) and 6px border-radius to match cards.

ui-bot: Reminder: upload updated token list to tokens repo after merge.

marta: I'll push branch feat/nocturne-theme with hatch variants. Once staging is up can someone run a deuteranopia simulation and axe pass?

sam: On it — will run accessibility checks after deploy. ETA 30-40m.

deploy-bot: build:staging triggered by marta — branch: feat/nocturne-theme — queued :rocket:

raj: If staging looks good, let's include the hatch as a toggle in storybook so QA can test both color-only and hatch+labels.

marta: Good plan. Thanks all — ping me for pairing on hatch tiling. :thumbsup:
